======================

This unexecuted metadata helper prepares the unchanged subset-pair worker in
shard mode. It borrows the actually reviewed endpoint pair (351 points, one
member) and selects only chunk000, ordinals [0,16), from the older consolidated
review of sixteen chunks. The selected provider has no external parent chunks.
Root must explicitly own its retained acyclic induction to d0 and the Original
bridge. This does not require or claim adoption of all3510 maps.

The helper reads scientific carriers, proofs, context and operands as opaque
bytes for exact hashes. It decodes only ordinary templates and accepted review
metadata. It never imports scientific Source, decodes points/maps/seed/witness
rows, computes a group action, invokes the worker, or writes canonical state.
The old Source-ownership record remains controls-only and unchanged. A separate
positive Root decision supplies all seven existing duties and selected-induction
ownership; the generated decision-bound import and gate apply to this one role.

All metadata afterimages are constructed and the complete read/write budget is
checked before creation of the fresh output directory. Files are exclusive,
fsynced, and read back whole; a partial filesystem failure leaves a visible
partial directory and is not silently retried or overwritten. The helper uses
the literal prior Ledger and serialization helpers. The new branch is metadata
assembly only, so no new numerical controls or old scientific replay is called
for. Independent Source review and a genuine Root metadata execution remain owed.

